msgid "4. Writing and transactions"
msgstr ""

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/12-databases.md:526
msgid "Work on a copy"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/12-databases.md:528
msgid "Never practise writes on a real database - and not on `data/portfolio.db` either. Make a copy: `con.backup` copies a whole SQLite database, even into memory:"
msgstr ""

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/12-databases.md:543
msgid "Create a table, insert rows, commit"
msgstr ""

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/12-databases.md:565
msgid "Transactions: all or nothing"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/12-databases.md:567
msgid "A **transaction** groups changes: either **all** of them are saved (`commit`) or **none** (`rollback`). The DB-API starts a transaction by itself before the first change; nothing is saved until `commit()`:"
msgstr ""

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/12-databases.md:586
msgid "`with con:` - commit or roll back by itself"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/12-databases.md:588
msgid "For `sqlite3`, a connection used in `with` **commits** at the end of the block - or **rolls back** if an exception happens inside. A payment run that must not be half done:"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/12-databases.md:610
msgid "The duplicate `P1` broke the **primary key**; the whole batch was rolled back - not two rows of three. In a monthly load, this is what you want: the table is either updated completely, or not at all."
msgstr ""

