#. box title
#: site/lectures/12-databases.md:648
msgid "SQL or Python?"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/12-databases.md:649
msgid "With a real database the data is on a server, often millions of rows. **Filter, join and aggregate in SQL** and take only the result into Python - the same idea as SAS pass-through. Python is the better place for the rules that are hard in SQL (text cleaning, checks with clear messages), for data from several sources, and for the report itself. More: [What to do in SQL, what in Python](#what-to-do-in-sql-what-in-python) in the Self-study part."
msgstr ""

